"""Targeted L12 r2 source comparisons; no personal eligibility service."""
UPDATES={
 'R06':('The applicable Florida community MSSI general disregard is $20 per month, not doubled for a couple, with the complete income-type exceptions retained. The February 24, 2026 DCF notice expressly excludes coverage groups based on long-term-care income standards (ICP, hospice, HCBS and PACE) and family-related Medicaid from that general disregard. The separate earned disregard remains $65 plus one-half of the remaining earned income. No universal $20 deduction is applied to all Medicaid budgets.', ['dcf-poverty-2026-r2:PAGE:1']),
 'R17':('All 22 January/April A-9.1 rows are retained. DCF I-26-02-0003, dated February 24, 2026 and effective April 1, 2026, supplies both tables and instructs April-and-ongoing mass-change processing for pending/open cases, with exact exception instructions. All 96 printed numeric cells agree with the previously retained tables. The December memo explains the interim 2.8% increase and no-closure safeguard. Published increments are used directly; no general rounding formula is invented.', ['dcf-poverty-2026-r2:PAGE:1','dcf-poverty-2026-r2:PAGE:3','dcf-poverty-2026-r2:PAGE:7']),
 'R19':('Florida QMB, SLMB and QI use the LIS-aligned family-size rule under DCF P-24-01-0001, dated January 26, 2024, effective upon receipt. Include the applicant, living-with spouse and co-resident relatives by blood, marriage or adoption dependent on the applicant/spouse for at least one-half support. The dependent relatives do not need Medicaid eligibility, and their income/assets are not counted. Individual/ineligible-spouse/eligible-couple counting and deeming remain; resource ceilings depend on eligible individual/couple status, not total family size. The memo supplies three explicit examples, a manual worksheet and system override instructions. This resolves the earlier overbroad warning against aligning Florida MSP family size with LIS, but does not transfer that family-size rule to every full-Medicaid category. Stale gender-specific wording is not a same-sex-marriage exclusion; SSA recognizes valid same-sex marriages in all states. Other marital/deeming facts remain case-specific.', ['dcf-msp-filing-unit-r2:PAGE:1','dcf-msp-filing-unit-r2:PAGE:2','dcf-msp-filing-unit-r2:PAGE:3','dcf-msp-filing-unit-r2:PAGE:5','ssa-marriage-r2:ALL','ssa-same-sex-r2:ALL']),
 'R28':('The dated December/February/May DCF notices establish January interim, April FPL and July spousal-standard transitions. The February 24 notice attachment already has the correct student amounts $2,410 monthly/$9,730 annual, agreeing with SSA and current DCF, unlike December attachment $2,416/$9,460. This is the earliest retained dated corrected table, not a located standalone erratum or proof of the first day DCF corrected individual cases. May 11 notice P-26-05-0003 explicitly directs $2,644 MMMNA/$794 shelter through June 30, 2026 and $2,705/$812 from July 1, with maximum CSMIA $4,067 unchanged through December 31. All 44 April and 44 July typed A-9 observations are compared. No historical personal award or case reprocessing is inferred.', ['dcf-poverty-2026-r2:PAGE:1','dcf-poverty-2026-r2:PAGE:6','dcf-spousal-2026-r2:PAGE:1','dcf-spousal-2026-r2:PAGE:2','dcf-spousal-2026-r2:PAGE:3']),
 'R30':('The published QMB baseline is coverage after the month of first QMB determination, rather than ordinary three-month retroactive Medicaid coverage. The retained CMS manual explicitly permits states to choose whether the determination month is the month all requirements were met or the actual decision month. New SSA guidance confirms the next-month rule and distinguishes retroactive processing from retroactive eligibility. No retained Florida instruction chooses between the two CMS options: the AHCA state-plan index returned HTTP 403 and was not retried, and the new DCF chapters/orders do not settle that election. Florida rule 65A-1.702 expressly provides SLMB/QI up to three months retroactive; CMS limits QI to the applicable calendar year. QMB-plus/non-QMB buy-in, premium Part A and processing/refund timing remain distinct. Exact Florida election is still held for agency/qualified confirmation.', ['ssa-qmb-139-r2:ALL']),
}

